    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nWith this PR, we can wait for screenshot by:\r\n```lua\r\n    opts.timeout = opts.timeout or 1000\r\n    opts.interval = opts.interval or 100\r\n    MiniTest.expect.reference_screenshot(\r\n      function() return child.get_screen_lines(screenshot_opts) end, path, opts)\r\n```\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-03-30T14:38:01Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nAs I've said in the ibhagwan/fzf-lua#1936, I don't really the pattern of \"wait unknown amount of time until the screen is like this\". Having an explicit wait time and known in advance checks seems to be more robust testing long term.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
