        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Another reason for not willing to support this is that it breaks the whole workflow around screenshot testing. Right now adding an `expect_screenshot()` call (in the way that it will be later used for testing) will create the reference screenshot file on the first run and compare to it on later ones. While \"wait for the right screenshot\" workflow requires an extra manual step for creating a reference screenshot (by writing essentially a different test code) and *then* replacing it with \"wait for the right one\" code.\r\n\r\nImplementing own helper outside of 'mini.test' internal methods should be still possible with something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal wait_for_screenshot = function(screenshot_name, timeout, interval)\r\n  interval = interval or 1\r\n  local screenshot_path = 'tests/screenshots/' .. screenshot_name\r\n  local ok, out\r\n  local predicate = function()\r\n    ok, out = pcall(MiniTest.expect.reference_screenshot, child.get_screenshot(), screenshot_path)\r\n    return ok\r\n  end\r\n  vim.wait(timeout, predicate, interval)\r\n  if ok then return end\r\n  -- Doesn't really report error right now. Might require a full\r\n  -- `new_expectation()` call.\r\n  error(out)\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nIts usage then requires creating a reference screenshot manually at a known path and using this helper to test it with \"wait for proper screen state\" workflow.",
            "created_at": "2025-03-30T14:59:06Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/1716#issuecomment-2764600219",
